      "id": "spann-tvshowfile-date",
      "repo": "Bas-Man/TVShowFile",
      "commit": "2f341c97dcbe52eee0c0e71752173c9e9442450c",
      "kind": "python-date",
      "tests": [
        "tests/Parser/600byDateJimmyFallon_test.py",
        "tests/Parser/610byDateStephenColbert_test.py",
        "tests/Parser/620byDateTMZonTV_test.py",
        "tests/Parser/630byDateJeopardy_test.py"
      ],
      "other": [
        "LICENSE",
        "README.md",
        "References.md",
        "setup.py",
        "tests/Parser/context.py"
      ],
      "flow": "Each setUp constructs Parser from one literal filename; a separate unittest assertion directly compares getCleanShowName() with a literal expected series title. context.py only imports local parser modules. No external fixture, constructor default name or actual output supplies the expected string. References.md lists regex/code references to tvregex, tvnamer and tvrenamr; none is a fixture import or expectation source in these four selected 2019 date tests. Only this fixed project's MIT tests and dependency notices are preserved; no referenced code or external data is imported. Date/title claims do not infer canonical seasons or episodes.",
